Done. Here’s a summary of the fix:[38;5;15m[1mBug[0m

The [38;5;10m`exportPDF`[39m function in [38;5;10m`script.js`[39m passed [38;5;10m`els.preview`[39m directly to [38;5;10m`html2pdf().from()`[39m. The library uses [38;5;10m`html2canvas`[39m internally, which needs to clone the source element and render it — but the cloned node was never attached to the document tree. Detached DOM nodes can’t resolve computed styles, layout, or CSS custom properties ([38;5;10m`var(--accent)`[39m, etc.), so the exported PDF would have missing/broken styling.[38;5;15m[1mChanges[0m[38;5;10m`script.js`[39m — [38;5;10m`exportPDF()`[39m:

• Clones [38;5;10m`els.preview`[39m with [38;5;10m`cloneNode(true)`[39m and adds the [38;5;10m`rp-export-clone`[39m class for off-screen positioning
• Appends the clone to [38;5;10m`document.body`[39m so it’s in the document tree (required by html2canvas)
• Renders from [38;5;10m`clone`[39m instead of [38;5;10m`els.preview`[39m
• Adds cleanup ([38;5;10m`document.body.removeChild(clone)`[39m) in [38;5;11m[1mboth[0m [38;5;10m`.then()`[39m (success) and [38;5;10m`.catch()`[39m (failure), with [38;5;10m`throw err`[39m in the catch to preserve error propagation[38;5;10m`style.css`[39m:

• Adds [38;5;10m`.rp-export-clone`[39m rule that positions the clone off-screen ([38;5;10m`left: -99999px`[39m, [38;5;10m`opacity: 0`[39m, [38;5;10m`z-index: -1`[39m, [38;5;10m`pointer-events: none`[39m) so it doesn’t flash on-screen during rendering, while still being in the DOM for style computation[38;5;15m[1mVerification[0m

